{
 "_doc": "c08 (critic A #1): early fills for legato targets whose samples sag 5-12 dB for their first 0.3 s at a flat CC11. {track: {score onset qn: dB}}: vol_db ramps 0 at onset - 0.02 qn to +dB at onset + 0.05 s, holds to + 0.35 s, back to 0 by + 0.6 s. Value = measured sag - 2, capped at 8. c09 (A #1): Ob1 55.5/57/271, CA 99/129.5/133.5, Fl1 190/252 added and Fl1 256 3 -> 5 (transition-sample holes of 8-10 dB at 1-2 semitone slurred steps, dB = pre-envelope dip - 3). c10 (A #2, A #4): a value may be {\"db\", \"pre_s\"}: 0 at onset - pre_s - 0.03 s, +db at onset - pre_s, held to onset + 0.10 s, 0 by + 0.35 s (holes that start before the score onset); its breakpoints are written exactly (parts.json vol_bp). Cl1 266, Fl1 270.5, Hn1 203 (pre_s), BCl 92.5, Ob1 270/142, CA 132, CA 133.5 4 -> 6; strings Vla 244/245.5/254.5, Vln II 59/60, Vc 77/86, Vln I 67.5. c11 (A #2, C #2): a dict value may carry \"hold_s\" (default 0.10): +db held to onset + hold_s, 0 by onset + hold_s + 0.25 s (holes longer than 0.10 s); pre_s defaults to 0. Bn1 231/262/269, Hn1 203 hold, Vln I 71/80/86, Vln II 65/66, CA 129.5/168, Ob1 142.5, Cl1 184/186, Vla 251.5; Horn 3 204 and Horn 2 210 (slow Ab4 Sus MAX attacks). After the c11 render: Horn 3 204 8 -> {8, hold 0.10} and Horn 2 210 6 -> {5, hold 0.22} (the plain 0.35 s hold put both 4-10 dB over their body at +0.3..+0.45 s, where the samples swell by themselves); applied to the rendered stems as a post-render envelope fix. c15 (A #2): Vc cantabile targets 74/75/246/247/249 (5-8 dB holes for 0.5 s, about 80% of the hole). c16: Ob1 271 7 -> 3 (B #1). c16 (C #2): tools/auto_fills.py 15 <c15 parts.json> measured every lead-line legato join on the c15 stems and wrote 110 entries (88 new, 22 raised); each is listed in its track's \"_auto\" key. Excluded: Ob1 271 (B #1 sets it to 3), Fl1 271 and Ob1 145.5 (B #1/#2 note trims). v600 port (series 2, c27, 2026-11-06): every onset key checked against v600 (pitch, length, the note before, printed dynamic, articulation); removed or moved: Flute 1 132, Flute 1 134, Flute 1 250, Flute 1 256, Flute 1 252, Flute 1 128, Flute 1 129.5, Flute 1 135, Flute 1 193, Flute 1 194, Oboe 1 145, Oboe 1 193, Clarinet 1 252, Clarinet 1 184, Clarinet 1 182, Clarinet 1 251.5, Bassoon 1 267, Bassoon 1 269, Horn 1 184, Horn 1 203, Horn 1 195, Horn 1 267, Horn 1 269, Horn 1 180, Horn 2 210, Bass clarinet 92.5, Bass clarinet 92, Bass clarinet 98, Bass clarinet 99, Bass clarinet 91.5, Violas 251.5, Violins II 59, Violoncellos 77, Violoncellos 247, Violoncellos 249, Violoncellos 157, Violoncellos 159, Violoncellos 160, Violoncellos 162, Violoncellos 219, Violoncellos 220, Violoncellos 267, Violoncellos 164, Violoncellos 180, Violins II div 108, Violas div 277 (moved to 279). c51: Flute 1 111 hold_s 0.30 (critic B #4); every dict fill on a note whose lead changed by 20 ms or more against c50 moved with its note-on (pre_s + d, hold_s - d; cycles/c51/actor_scripts/fillshift51.py). c52: 76 dict fills on notes whose lead changed by 20 ms or more against c51 moved with their note-on (cycles/c52/actor_scripts/fillshift52.py). c53: 4 dict fills on notes whose lead changed by 20 ms or more against c52 moved with their note-on (cycles/c53/actor_scripts/fillshift53.py).",
